The other difficulty I have with this approach is I'm unsure of the right way to efficiently generate samples from y in the generated quantities block, since the lognormal distribution doesn't do it. Do I need an if-then-else structure to first generate a z, and then set y = 1 if z = 1, or sample from the lognormal if z = 0? Or is there a better way?

