Hi,

I have estimated a Hidden Markov Model (HMM) for animal movement states (with the help of Bob! See the attached.) The marginalisation of the latent states is handled via dynamic programming using the forwards/backwards algorithm.

I have a number of model permutations which I would like to compare using some measure of predictive performance. For example, I would like to compare a two-state HMM with a three-state one.

My question is - does anyone have any ideas how to estimate WAIC (or LOO-CV) without repeatedly partitioning the data into T-1 points and a single datum? The model takes about half an hour to estimate for ~18,000 data points, and so doing this for all points is clearly not feasible.

Best,

Ben

