Well, LOO can be appropriate for time series, but not always. Depends on what you're focused on, e.g. it's ok if you are considering the ability of the model to describe the structure in the observed time series. But if you're focused on prediction for new data, then yes some form of sequential cross-validation seems ideal (but I thought too computationally demanding in this case. How big is T?). If you do try sequential cross-validation then I would probably condition on at least several data points, i.e. don't start with t = 2.

