At first glance it looks like you've declared it but not given it a value. Then when you have the "~" statement it tries to compute the log density at the value on the left of the "~", which isn't going to work if it doesn't yet have a value. You'll either need to declare that variable as an unknown parameter in the parameters block, or keep it in the model block but give it a value. If it's something you're trying to estimate then the former and if it's observed (or a function of observed variables) then the latter.

Hope that helps,

Jonah

