> On Tuesday, July 12, 2016 at 2:07:53 PM UTC-4, Krzysztof Sakrejda wrote:
> > I'd also be careful about the log-normal priors since they can imply a pretty big upper tail (for example, that lognormal(log(400),5) prior if you simulate a thousand draws will regularly generate values in the 10^8 range which is going to cause computational problems in an ODE model unless there is enough data to make the posterior much tighter.
>
> Not implying that Stan is drawing from the prior at all, it's just an indicator of the prior not doing much to restrain the space that Stan has to sample from.
>
